    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft",
    "tactics": "Shadows avoid bright light and exploit dim areas. They stack Strength Drain against a single target, attempting to reduce them to 0 Strength. A Summoner who calls one should be prepared for it to ignore tactical nuance in favor of finding the darkest spot in the room and hunting from there.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Strength Drain [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 2), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 6 Negative damage (4 + 2 Str) + target's Strength reduced by 1 for 1 hour.</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 6 Negative damage, DR halved (round up) + Strength reduced by 2 for 1 hour + target makes Fortitude [Easy] save  or gains the Weakened condition.</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Shadow Form: While in dim light or darkness, the Shadow has DR 8 against all non-magical damage. Positive-energy damage ignores this entirely. Amorphous: The Shadow can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch. Sunlight Weakness: In bright light, the Shadow has Misfortune on all rolls. Shadow Spawn: If a non-undead creature is killed by Strength Drain-induced Strength reduction (Strength reduced to 0), it rises as a Shadow under the controlling summoner's influence at the start of its next turn.</p>",
